# 00_common.kzm -- the predict model of profile c1-bp-b051eb0 (format kzp-predict 1; kairos/docs/predict.md): the cone of
# the verified C1 scope.  Read with one CF revision file (cf-281a941.kzm or cf-833fdbb.kzm) and the profile directories
# of `kz replay` (this directory, cf-<REV>/, bundle-<CAND>/, rspec-<REV>/); it states no condition of a run.
#
# Actors: the initial thread of the process (core-tx: start state, task creation, teardown), the ES main task (the
# shutdown request: an external input, the harness's restart command), the CF main task (the dependent lookups), the
# BP main task (the existence probes and the creations).  Resources: the two counting semaphores by name (the table's
# names) and the shutdown state.  Every other actor and object of the record is outside the cone; kz predict lists
# them and refuses the prediction if one of them touches a key of the cone.
#
# Orders kept as constraints: program order inside each actor (r_axiom_program_order), task creation (R2-P-TASK: a
# task's first event follows its creating call), the creation order of the startup thread (core apps, then the start
# script line by line: m_es_core_then_script, m_es_script_line, bp_startup_script; CF before BP), the poll of the
# startup thread for the shutdown request (psp_teardown).  No source orders CF's and BP's steps against each other:
# no startup-sync call in CF or BP, ES's global-state waits block only ES, priorities not applied
# (plan/C1_basis_plan.md section 6.2).  The OSAL object-table locks make each lookup, creation and deletion one atomic
# step at its linearization point (osal_get_by_name, osal_convert_token_global: the search under the type's global
# lock; osal_allocate_new, osal_transaction_finish: creation and deletion in EXCLUSIVE transactions); they order no
# two calls.  Not modelled (not explored): the RESERVED window inside a creation (A5 of P-C1HOLD), other creation
# failures (no free ids, implementation errors), a deletion other than the teardown's (no application of the closure
# deletes these names; CF's exit cleans up only the objects CF's task created: m_es_cleanup_task, m_osal_creator,
# m_osal_foreach_creator; BP does not exit in the cone), the time of any step.
kzp-predict 1

